Subject: [PATCH 4/4] misc/rasdaemon.service.in: also require the tracefs mount

Commit 2507a210c905 ("rasdaemon requires debugfs - add dependency to
rasdaemon.service") makes the service require /sys/kernel/debug. But
rasdaemon reads its events from tracefs and looks for it first:
debugfs is only the fallback through the deprecated debugfs/tracing
automount, and holds the ras/daemon_active file of the extlog handler.
On a kernel without DEBUG_FS, or one that no longer automounts tracefs
under debugfs, the events are only at /sys/kernel/tracing, which the
unit does not wait for.

Require both mount points. On such a kernel sys-kernel-debug.mount
fails its ConditionPathExists= and is skipped, which does not stop the
service from starting.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01N8fTR5eZWWPFd2fewTXKDt
Signed-off-by: Fco Javier Felix <ffelix@inode64.com>
---
 misc/rasdaemon.service.in | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/misc/rasdaemon.service.in b/misc/rasdaemon.service.in
index 4aeb7f0..4355794 100644
--- a/misc/rasdaemon.service.in
+++ b/misc/rasdaemon.service.in
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 Description=RAS daemon to log the RAS events
 # only needed when not running in foreground (--foreground | -f)
 #After=syslog.target
-RequiresMountsFor=/sys/kernel/debug
+RequiresMountsFor=/sys/kernel/debug /sys/kernel/tracing
 
 [Service]
 EnvironmentFile=@SYSCONFDEFDIR@/rasdaemon
